## Session summary

**Landed and validated:** Root-caused and fixed the primary `dlm_scaling@32` blocker — `find_slot()` can never report a tombstone as "found" (its contract only matches live slots), so the epoch-reset call session 7 built was silently no-op'ing 100% of the time regardless of hook placement. Real fix: threaded an `is_free` flag into `mxfs_dlm_caw_unlock_gen()` so the epoch clear piggybacks on the unlock's own existing tombstone CAS — zero extra I/O. Aggregate dlm_scaling throughput went from a historical ~1319-1650 ops/s ceiling to a stable ~1794-1805 ops/s, with two clean 32/32 passes observed. Also landed a secondary fix for a shortform-directory content-staleness gap at sf→block conversion time (extended `mxfs_dir_modify_adopt_disk_format`'s check, re-enabled its previously-disabled call site).

**Investigated but reverted:** Attempted to fix `cache_coherency@32`'s "uv gone" dangling-dirent bug (a well-documented, previously 16-node-diagnosed Case-B mechanism) by making the xfsaild dir-block clobber guard bidirectional. This regressed `posix_multi@8/caw` (renamed content came back empty, a hardlink disappeared) — confirmed as a real regression by reverting and rebuilding back to the identical prior srcversion. Root cause of the unsafety is understood and documented: a count/checksum-only comparison can't distinguish a genuinely stale peer buffer from a legitimate async post-release destage of our own correctly-dirtied work. Tree is back to a clean, safe build (VERSION 0.10.104, srcversion `C9D0F29C6FCADEAF836A132`) with no partial edits.

**Remaining work**, all detailed in memory `AAA-ccloopcc87-sess8-END-cachecoh-bidirectional-clobber-REVERTED`: a correct fix for cache_coherency's dangling-dirent bug (needs per-entry provenance, not aggregate counts); running the 12 of 17 32-node criteria that have never completed a real pass; and a final 1/2/4/8/16-node regression pass. Criteria are **not yet met** — 32-node caw is closer but not at 100%.

